<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 442)</h2>
<p><b>The wave is part of the note.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Voice notes now record your pointer.</b> Wave the cursor at the thing you're talking about — playback retraces it as an orange ring, in time with your voice, on every seat. Movie exports that hold on voice notes burn the pointer in too: frozen frame, voice, and the ring circling what it circled.</li>
<li><b>Paste a session key anywhere.</b> The Shared Review panel now takes a review link (or the bare session id and key) on every build — paste and Join, nothing else to configure. Open Link recognizes review links too.</li>
<li><b>Export All Annotated Frames covers the whole session</b> — every clip's marked frames, each rendered through its own grade and looks. Tick "Current clip only" to narrow it.</li>
<li>Fixed: live presence (pointers and in-progress strokes from shared-session peers) never actually rendered in the native viewport. It does now.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
