</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 441)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: a clip's remembered input space could be silently overwritten during playlist playback</b> — a race at clip switches wrote the incoming clip's space under the outgoing clip's format, so (for example) an EXR sequence would drift to a video transform as a compare looped. The per-format memory now records your explicit picks only. If a format looks wrong after updating, pick its space once and it sticks again.</li>
<li><b>Marks align in side-by-side and stacked compares</b>: each picture shows its own marks, and drawing targets the picture under your cursor — left is A, right is B, wherever the A|B toggle sits. A stroke that starts on one picture stays on it across the split. (The text tool still wants a full-frame view.)</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
